/** @page logger_binreleasehistory logger_bin Module Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    This module is always delivered with %Qore and therefore mirrors the %Qore version.

    @section logger_bin_3_0 logger_bin Module Version 3.0

    @ref Qore::Logger::LoggerAppenderFile "LoggerAppenderFile" raises \c FILE-OPEN2-ERROR when it opens a file name
    with a NUL character instead of opening the file named by the name cut at the NUL character, and raises only
    \c APPENDER-OPEN-ERROR when the file name is not a string.

    Logger interface deserialization restores its native callback adapter. Logger wrappers and
    schema objects inheriting the interface can be serialized repeatedly after restoration.

    A @ref Qore::Logger::Logger "Logger" references its appenders where the garbage collector can follow the
    references, so a cycle through an appender that references its logger is collected instead of being leaked with
    the classes of its objects.  An event created by a logger references the logger:
    @ref Qore::Logger::LoggerEvent::getLogger() "LoggerEvent::getLogger()" read freed memory for an event kept after
    its logger was destroyed.

    An appender references its layout and filters, and an event its level, arguments and exception information, where
    the garbage collector can follow the references, so a cycle through any of them is collected.

    A message can be logged as it is, with no formatting, with
    @ref Qore::Logger::Logger::logPreformatted() "Logger::logPreformatted()" and
    @ref Qore::Logger::LoggerInterface::logPreformatted() "LoggerInterface::logPreformatted()": the other logging
    methods use the message as a format, so that a message with format characters lost them
    (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/3420">issue 3420</a>).

    A @ref Qore::Logger::Logger "Logger" is serialized with its level and parent: they were left out, so a
    deserialized logger had no level of its own (qore#6839).

    The file, file name and encoding of a @ref Qore::Logger::LoggerAppenderFile "LoggerAppenderFile" are
    \c private:internal: a subclass uses @ref Qore::Logger::LoggerAppenderFile::getFile() "getFile()",
    @ref Qore::Logger::LoggerAppenderFile::getFileName() "getFileName()" and
    @ref Qore::Logger::LoggerAppenderFile::setFileName() "setFileName()" instead of the members (qore#6839).
*/
